From cab4dde9b895ee75c31f69aa78baf6b2baa63a3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:30:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/20] qwen3_5 HIP: SenseNova-Loop's mHC kernels, their own
 image and their contract

The four mHC kernels land as the ops/mhc.hip group, a mechanical port
of the SenseNova recipe's CUDA qwen35_mhc.cu into the HIP house style:
the router routes 16/S rows a block (each row's norm scaling its dots
after, the router's weights and the row read once), twenty log-space
Sinkhorn passes fix the 2x2 mix, pre and post pass sigmoids, and the
state's coefficients are read back through bf16 as the reference
weights are. The merge folds a sublayer's output into the streams with
the mix and post a (row, column) a thread; enter and leave move the
residual in and its mean out. hipcc has not run here yet: the image
compiles in phase B, with the code object this stub build already
shapes.

Their contract runs the five cases at the served width (the router's
branch and state, merge, enter, leave) against the FP64 reference the
CUDA contract computes, with a planted control each: the branch without
its row norm, the state without Sinkhorn, the merge as an identity map,
the enter without its fold and the leave over one stream. Gate-5 launch
records wait for a real gfx1103 compile, as every record must.

hip.zig's source table moves to hip_sources.zig to keep the build file
inside its 600-line cap.
